-- statement:
--   An auxiliary lemma of the round-six development, published as a separate node because its proof is long or shared.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `R6Pk.R6BitNBNetE`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.Bit.NB.DC_vals : (List.range 23).map DC = [2668, 45080, 26286, 8326, 12804, 9110, 3607, 3026, 3285, 2451,
--       3515, 1255, 3239, 1600, 3308, 1968, 4159, 1255, 10043, 3926, 1288, 2750, 3565]
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, bit network: the child-width histogram and `BitNetR6MomStmt`
--
--   Every edge of the network contributes the moment of its runs: side edges of rank `r` give
--   `f (2r - 23) + (23 - r) f 1` (`2r > 23`) or `r f 1`, aux edges `f 23 + f 483`, data edges
--   `f 439 + f 21 + 24 f 1`. The per-rank move counts of the two stage words are the base-`2³²` digits
--   of the kernel-checked packed counts `CNs1`, `CNs2` (no overflow: `touch1`, `touch2`). The total
--   moment equals Jain's `bitR6` moment.
--
